  "voice_script": "[curious] That blue USB port may be lying...\nBlue usually signals SuperSpeed, while black often points to USB 2.0.\nSo blue means faster, right?\n[surprised] Not ALWAYS!\n\n[serious] USB 2.0 reaches 480 megabits per second; newer ports may advertise 5, 10, 20, 40, or 80 gigabits.\n[skeptical] But color is only a clue...\nThe standards group recommends blue for USB 3.0 Standard-A, but allows other ways to distinguish ports.\nWhat should you trust?\n\n[curious] Check the SS logo, then read the specification.\n[serious] Charging's separate; color doesn't tell you wattage.\n[curious] What about USB-C? Its shape doesn't guarantee speed or power.\n\n[softly] The free guide and our community link are in the description.\n[curious] Follow the channel for tech tips!\n\n[quietly] Blue is a hint... the specification is the ANSWER."
